<title>USA: FGIC qualifies nine issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies nine issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>FGIC said Thursday it qualified for bond insurance the following nine municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Hartford, Conn., $25 million of GO bonds.</p>
<p>--Newtown, Conn., $34.315 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Cecil County, Md., $8.840 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Franklin County Unified School District No 290, Kan., $9.675 million GO school bonds.</p>
<p>--Evesham Board of Education, N.J., $17.69 million bonds.</p>
<p>--Palm Beach Gardens, Fla., $4.4 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Las Vegas, Nev., $36.725 million GO sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--Holmdel Township Board of Education, N.J., $9.7 million of school bonds.</p>
<p>--Cheatham County, Tenn., $16 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
